{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"length","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","reasoning_content":"We need count binary strings length 12 that avoid forbidden substrings \"111\" and \"000\". So no three consecutive same bits. Count sequences with no run of 3 identical bits. This is classic combinatorics. We can use recurrence: Let a_n be number of sequences length n ending with run of length 1 of some bit, b_n ending with run length 2. Actually we need track last two bits maybe. Let's define states: ending with ...0, run length 1 of 0; ending with ...00, run length 2 of 0; similarly for 1. But symmetry. Let A_n = sequences length n ending with a single 0 (i.e., last bit 0, previous bit 1 or start). B_n = ending with two 0s (last two bits 00). Similarly C_n for single 1, D_n for two 1s. Recurrence: A_{n+1} = C_n + D_n (since to end with single 0, previous bit must be 1). B_{n+1} = A_n (since to end with two 0s, previous must be single 0). Similarly C_{n+1} = A_n + B_n. D_{n+1} = C_n. Base n=1: sequences length1: \"0\" -> A_1=1, B_1=0; \"1\" -> C_1=1, D_1=0. Compute up to n=12.\n\nLet's iterate.\n\nn=1: A=1,B=0,C=1,D=0. total=2.\n\nn=2:\nA2 = C1 + D1 =1+0=1\nB2 = A1 =1\nC2 = A1 + B1 =1+0=1\nD2 = C1 =1\nTotals: A+B+C+D=1+1+1+1=4. Check all 4 strings length2: 00,01,10,11. All allowed.\n\nn=3:\nA3 = C2 + D2 =1+1=2\nB3 = A2 =1\nC3 = A2 + B2 =1+1=2\nD3 = C2 =1\nTotal=2+1+2+1=6. Let's list: 001,010,011,100,101,110. Indeed 000 and 111 excluded.\n\nn=4:\nA4 = C3 + D3 =2+1=3\nB4 = A3 =2\nC4 = A3 + B3 =2+1=3\nD4 = C3 =2\nTotal=3+2+3+2=10.\n\nn=5:\nA5 = C4 + D4 =3+2=5\nB5 = A4 =3\nC5 = A4 + B4 =3+2=5\nD5 = C4 =3\nTotal=5+3+5+3=16.\n\nn=6:\nA6 = C5 + D5 =5+3=8\nB6 = A5 =5\nC6 = A5 + B5 =5+3=8\nD6 = C5 =5\nTotal=8+5+8+5=26.\n\nn=7:\nA7 = C6 + D6 =8+5=13\nB7 = A6 =8\nC7 = A6 + B6 =8+5=13\nD7 = C6 =8\nTotal=13+8+13+8=42.\n\nn=8:\n"}}],"created":1790959356,"model":"C:\\Users\\d2j3\\Documents\\Codex\\2026-09-10\\napraw\\outputs\\moon-native\\models\\gpt-oss-20b-MXFP4.gguf